net: airoha: PPE insert orientation probe (201-07 / 941)

Follow-up to 940 (PPE bind=0 diagnostics).  The 940 first field test
(build-26) showed the promotion chain breaks inside
airoha_ppe_foe_insert_entry(): ~96% "no sw match" (software pending
table compare failure), 4% state mismatch, zero commits, bind stays 0.

Offline comparison against lotusmomo/airoha_sdk + mainline
mediatek/mtk_ppe.c (report: airoha-sdk对拍报告-20107方向_20261017.md)
narrowed the suspect set to:

- compare_entry() memcmps only the 12-byte orig_tuple
  (src_ip + dest_ip + ports), so a mismatch means tuple *content*,
  not MAC/PPPoE metadata.
- The bucket index is recomputed from the *hardware-learned* entry
  tuple via airoha_ppe_foe_get_entry_hash(), and that hash function is
  src/dst-asymmetric — a reversed tuple fails twice (wrong bucket +
  wrong memcmp).
- Leading hypothesis C1: on a PPPoE WAN the first RX packets the PPE
  learns from are the *replies* (WAN->LAN), i.e. the hardware tuple is
  the reverse of the software table's FLOW_ORIG tuple.  __mtk_ppe_check_skb
  does not recompute the hash from the tuple (uses the descriptor hash),
  which is why the MTK sibling does not hit this.

This patch instruments only the compare-failure branch of
airoha_ppe_foe_insert_entry() (depends on 940, must sort after it):

1. Two-way tuple dump: "insert: mismatch sw=%pI4:%04x>%pI4:%04x
   hw=%pI4:%04x>%pI4:%04x ib1=%08x" — ports printed as raw BE entry
   words (no byte-order interpretation) so the log can be read side by
   side with the SW table.  IPv4 ROUTE/HNAPT only; other type combos
   get a counter line ("insert: mismatch non-ipv4 etype/htype").
2. Reversed-match trial: on mismatch, swap src/dst ip + ports in a
   stack copy of the hw entry and run compare_entry() again — a hit
   prints "insert: REVERSED match" and proves/disproves C1 with zero
   guessing.
3. Bucket empty/non-empty split: "insert: bucket empty hash=%x
   index=%u" fires when the software bucket held no candidate at all
   (points at the replace-refusal path) vs the existing
   "insert: no sw match" (bucket had entries but none matched —
   direction/byte-order territory).  Also covers the 4% non-IPv4
   suspects as countable lines.

Diagnostic only — no functional change.  Same runtime switch as 940:
  echo 0 > /sys/module/airoha_eth/parameters/ppe_dbg_enabled

On-device verification (same discipline as 940: real TCP download,
never ping):
  dmesg | grep 20106
Judgement keys:
  "REVERSED match" present      -> C1 confirmed; fix = orientation-aware
                                   lookup in insert (SW entry is
                                   authoritative, commit overwrites the
                                   whole 64B slot anyway).
  mismatch dumps with equal-looking tuples -> byte-order/port-field
                                   layout issue in the entry words.
  "bucket empty" dominant       -> flows never reach the SW pending
                                   table; back to replace-side gates.

Generated against vanilla v6.18.52 + huladabang/ponwrt@c3b518b airoha
series + 940 applied.  Applies after 940 (941 sorts right behind it).
Validated: patch(940) -> git apply(941) forward and reverse, zero
reject both directions.
